  "output": {
    "answer": "It's the panel talking, not a usability lab. The 9-seconds-per-task figure for Dez came from simulated personas walking fixtures, not a human being timed on a real device — the record is explicit that those numbers are simulated. So it's the agents' own read of the screen, dressed up as a task time. And the gate that produced it then failed the real test: my own phone the next morning showed the app was basically unusable, which the panel's fixed-viewport walk hadn't caught. I wouldn't call 9 seconds a usability number in the normal sense — it's an agent's self-report.",
